# React Security

## XSS via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`

Treat every usage as a review halt. Prefer text or sanitized markdown. If raw HTML is required, sanitize at the call site (e.g. DOMPurify).

## Unsafe URL Schemes

Validate `http:`, `https:`, `mailto:` before putting user-controlled values in `href` / `src`.

## `target="_blank"`

Always pair with `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.

## Server Actions / tRPC Mutations

Same trust level as a public API:

- Zod-validate every input
- Authenticate/authorize inside the mutation when mutating protected data
- Never trust client-only gates

## Env Vars

| Kind | Examples |
|---|---|
| Public | `NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_CDN_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` |
| Server-only | `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` |

Audit every new `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` — it ships to the browser.

## Auth Storage

Prefer httpOnly cookies for sessions. Do not store secrets in `localStorage`.
